.TH LS 1 "October 2026" "ls-v1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ls \- list directory contents (OS Assignment 02 re-implementation)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ls
[\fB\-lxR\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the contents of each DIRECTORY (default: current directory). Hidden files (names beginning with a dot) are not shown. Output is sorted alphabetically and colorized when writing to a terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Long listing format: permissions, link count, owner, group, size, modification time, name.
.TP
.B \-x
Display entries in columns, left to right (horizontal), instead of down then across.
.TP
.B \-R
List subdirectories recursively.
.SH COLORS
Blue: directories. Green: executables. Red: archives (.tar, .gz, .zip). Pink: symbolic links. Reverse video: special files.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by ROLL_NO for the Operating Systems course.
